<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kalkar</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kalkar is a town on the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-rhine-westphalia">North Rhine-Westphalia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, founded by the counts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kleve">Cleves</a> in 1230. It prospered from the cloth trade in the late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>, when its church of St Nicolai was furnished with carved altarpieces by a renowned school of local woodcarvers. It is also known for a nuclear power station that was completed but never operated and is now an amusement park.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kalkar.jpg" alt="Kalkar" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Michielverbeek · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kalkar,_monumentaal_pand_2006-09-10_15.21.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
